formats.c: don't #error on substrate's unknown FILE layout.

rewind_pipe() pokes libc-internal FILE fields to rewind a pipe a few
bytes (for file-type autodetection on pipes), and #errors on a libc it
doesn't recognise.  substrate's stdio isn't BSD/glibc/MSVC-shaped; per
the upstream comment, dropping the #error just disables pipe file-type
detection, which is acceptable.

--- a/src/formats.c
+++ b/src/formats.c
@@ -419,7 +419,7 @@ static void UNUSED rewind_pipe(FILE * fp)
 #else
   /* To fix this #error, either simply remove the #error line and live without
    * file-type detection with pipes, or add support for your compiler in the
    * lines above.  Test with cat monkey.wav | ./sox --info - */
-  #error FIX NEEDED HERE
+  /* substrate: unknown FILE layout -> no pipe rewind */
   #define NO_REWIND_PIPE
   (void)fp;
 #endif
